    "answer": {
        "text": "§\nAdverse Effects (4) : Bleomycin\n\n(1) Pulmonary toxicity\n(2) Skin toxicity\n\n(3) Stomatitis/Mucositis\n\n(4) Alopecia\n\n(Bleomycin is activated by oxygen ∴ highly oxygenated environment of lung predisposes to collateral damage)\n\n[Image: fb71b5cf323f6001fe93b0ac029cafcc2bd08ab9e03496832f559825d2b3d010]\n\n[Image: edffafcf1984e445c0d4e0f91e1df9bce4af7db401742a71dbedd66115ec99e4]\n\n[Image: 9ecdfb1ded8ae0e86cffabc256e2b41900e6bfea3a22de9c0b00a96f388cb89d]\n\n2.3 - Bleomycin, doxorubicin, daunorubicin, actinomycin D\n[Image: d837b2ec4413cf7fca8a7c2eb4363f3ce0310892d5aef0467164ba5e4e896967]\n\n[Image: 16c44e405d839f2f3af173c3bea7fbd7a55058f769d085ae38803085248ffc91]",
